# Shopify Skeleton Theme — Project Overview

## What this is

A minimalist, Theme-Store-ready Shopify theme with a TypeScript + Vite build pipeline. Intentionally small and foundational — not a fully-featured theme.

## Architecture

```
layout/            # theme.liquid (main), password.liquid
sections/          # Liquid sections with {% schema %} — the core UI units
snippets/          # Reusable Liquid partials (pdp-*, header-*, product-card, etc.)
blocks/            # Nestable theme blocks (group.liquid, text.liquid)
templates/         # JSON templates (index, product, collection, cart, blog, etc.)
config/            # settings_schema.json + settings_data.json
locales/           # Translation JSON
assets/            # Static files + Vite output (theme.js, theme.css, critical.css)
src/scripts/       # TypeScript source → compiled to assets/theme.js
src/styles/        # SCSS source → compiled to assets/theme.css
src/types/         # TypeScript declarations (shopify.d.ts)
docs/              # Internal development docs
```

## Build system

- **Vite** (`vite.config.ts`): single entry `src/scripts/theme.ts` → `assets/theme.js` (IIFE)
- SCSS compiled through Vite; `loadPaths: ['src/styles']` enables bare `@use` imports
- `emptyOutDir: false` — Vite writes to `assets/` without deleting other files
- `npm run dev` = `concurrently "shopify theme dev" "vite build --watch"`
- `npm run build` = production Vite build

## Key dependencies

- **gsap** — all JS animations (drawer slide, submenu reveal, hero transitions)
- **swiper** — carousels/sliders (hero, product gallery thumbs)
- **@shopify/cli** — theme dev server, theme check, packaging

## Code formatting

- Prettier: no semicolons, single quotes, 2-space indent, trailing commas (es5)
- ESLint: `@typescript-eslint/recommended`, `no-explicit-any: warn`
- TypeScript: strict mode, ES2020 target, bundler module resolution

## Section registration pattern

Every interactive section follows this flow:
1. Define `registerXxxSection()` in `src/scripts/xxx.ts`
2. Call `registerSection(SECTION_TYPE, init, destroy)` from section-registry
3. Import and call `registerXxxSection()` in `theme.ts`
4. Liquid section uses `data-section-type="xxx"` and `data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"`
5. `bootSections()` auto-inits on DOMContentLoaded; MutationObserver catches dynamically added sections
6. Shopify editor events (`shopify:section:load/unload`) handled automatically

## Liquid conventions

- Sections expose settings via `{% schema %}` JSON
- CSS variables on section root for dynamic settings: `style="--gap: {{ block.settings.gap }}px"`
- Prefer `{% stylesheet %}` / `{% javascript %}` for co-located section CSS/JS
- Critical CSS in `assets/critical.css`; non-critical via Vite (`assets/theme.css`)
- Font loading via `snippets/font-pairing-loader.liquid` in `<head>`
- Cart routes set in `layout/theme.liquid` as `window.__themeRoutes` (preferred over `Shopify.routes`)

## When editing this project

- Always check `data-section-type` matches between Liquid and TypeScript
- Run `npm run check` (Theme Check) after Liquid changes
- Run `npm run build` after TypeScript/SCSS changes to verify compilation
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` in all JS animations
- Use AbortController for section cleanup in `destroy()` functions
